"upon","H935":"come","H5650":"servant/slave","H413":"to(wards)","H776":"country/planet","H8269":"ruler","H3513":"honour","H853":"[Obj.]","H5869":"eye","H3808":"not","H5668":"for the sake of","H2713":"to search","H2015":"to overturn","H7270":"to spy","H3947":"take","H1548":"to shave","H3772":"cut","H4063":"garment","H2677":"half","H5704":"till","H4667":"hip","H3212":"to walk","H5046":"to tell","H376":"man","H7125":"befall","H3637":"be humiliated","H3966":"much","H3427":"to dwell","H3405":"Jericho","H834":"which","H6779":"to spring","H2206":"beard","H7725":"return","H7200":"see","H887":"to stink","H505":"thousand","H3603":"Plain (of Jericho)","H3701":"money","H7936":"to hire","H4480":"from","H763":"Mesopotamia","H758":"Aram","H4601":"Maacah","H6678":"Zobah","H7393":"chariot","H6571":"horse","H8147":"two","H7970":"thirty","H5971":"people","H2583":"to camp","H6440":"before","H4311":"Medeba","H622":"to gather","H5892":"excitement","H4421":"battle","H8085":"hear","H3097":"Joab","H3605":"all","H6635":"army","H1368":"mighty man","H3318":"come","H6186":"to arrange","H6607":"entrance","H905":"pole","H7704":"Sirion","H268":"back","H977":"to choose","H3478":"Israel","H3499":"remainder","H5414":"give","H3027":"hand","H52":"Abishai","H251":"male-sibling","H518":"if","H2388":"strengthen","H8668":"salvation","H3467":"to save","H1157":"about/through/for","H430":"God","H3068":"LORD","H2896":"pleasant","H5066":"approach","H5127":"to flee","H1571":"also","H1992":"they(masc.)","H3389":"Jerusalem","H5062":"to strike","H5676":"beside","H5104":"River","H7780":"Shophach","H1909":"Hadadezer","H5674":"to pass","H3383":"Jordan","H3898":"to fight","H2026":"to kill","H7651":"seven","H705":"forty","H7273":"on foot","H7999":"to complete","H5647":"to serve","H14":"be willing","H5750":"still"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["challoner",18,null,"challoner","Seven thousand chariots.... That is, of men who fought in chariots."],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Land, or city, 2 Kings x. 3. (Calmet) — What evils proceed from evil counsellors!"],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","From. Hebrew, “in the midst, above the thighs:” exposing them to derision. (Haydock)"],["haydock",6,null,"haydock","Done. Hebrew, “made themselves stinking.” Septuagint, “that the people of David was covered with confusion.” The insult fell on all Israel. — Mesopotamia is not mentioned [in] 2 Kings, as the troops perhaps did not arrive soon enough for the first battle, ver. 16."],["haydock",7,null,"haydock","Chariots. This number seems excessive, and it may have been put for infantry; the number of which, specified [in] 2 Kings, was 33,000. But the troops of Mesopotamia are not there mentioned, and this supplies what was left defective. (Calmet) — The chariots may signify those who fought upon them, (Menochius) ver. 18., and Isaias xxi. 7. (Tirinus) — Sometimes the whole number is specified; at others only a part."],["haydock",16,null,"haydock","River, in Mesopotamia. Joab did not allow them time to arrive. — Sophach, or Sobac. Adarezer sent also to collect these forces, 2 Kings."],["haydock",18,null,"haydock","Chariots. Literally, “chariot.” 2 Kings has only 700, and 40,000 horsemen. (Calmet) — Ten men might be in each chariot. (Du Hamel)"],["haydock",19,null,"haydock","Went. Hebrew, “made peace with David.” The many petty kings who had hitherto been tributary to Adarezer, submitted now to the conqueror. (Calmet)"]],"au":{"challoner":["Richard Challoner",0,0,1781,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/03566a.htm"],"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}